#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119433 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/id #uuid "9bd80a60-0f80-5cc2-8193-86fb32c79913" :question/math-academy-id "e-12467" :question/problem "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4y-2{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =4y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119434 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/id #uuid "51e74bbf-6ce4-58c4-84b1-44a2f4c46ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-12468" :question/problem "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3 , 1\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =1+3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1+3\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} =  \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,1)} & =\\frac{1}{1+3\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119435 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/id #uuid "330c7f67-4c32-5ab7-9909-1835bba1b1f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12469" :question/problem "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}-y+1) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-1+0 \\\\  & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4b442c9-5e3f-59c0-a5fc-d93fbce1d127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15y-10{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285863} {:answer/id #uuid "5f413ed0-0bd4-5174-90fc-1bae17195a8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{y}^{2}-20y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285864} {:answer/id #uuid "21e67c4d-c773-5317-b3c5-4a502c205209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3y-20{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285865} {:answer/id #uuid "6faeca04-7056-5bc7-8ef4-5eb4106f6aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285866} {:answer/id #uuid "97afb73d-0d64-5072-b81b-1c0d4409a9fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}-10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6faeca04-7056-5bc7-8ef4-5eb4106f6aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285866} :answer-field/id #uuid "5774f4fc-5433-5265-b747-7e504a314afc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d402a78d-7baa-5a8f-a1ce-6df24cc00d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-109156" :question/problem "If $x=5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-20y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad4c99bb-8b6d-5c67-b6c4-90de5961e269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{18}-\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285870} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf3f0f0-a6ce-5d6c-a030-c21bec510897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285871} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc6a547-b739-57dc-a6b9-8a02dc338d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285872} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e323f8-7582-56ac-a835-3a7822270a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285873} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ccaf33-86cc-52d8-b71c-5f6edbaa24b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1e323f8-7582-56ac-a835-3a7822270a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285873} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cfa6d9-bc03-5e11-a377-d13e974df5f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb002c1f-25a0-5470-9804-c9c0192129f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-110192" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (3{y}^{2})-8\\cdot (2y)+0 \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-16y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-16y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(24,2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\cdot {2}^{2}-16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{28}(x-24) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}-\\frac{6}{7}+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2cabd18-a447-5eca-921f-3c5b8790f2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285877} {:answer/id #uuid "e24a8405-b039-5026-bb8d-d473cee99488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285878} {:answer/id #uuid "514daf85-79c9-5f75-b7a8-a3556a0a0463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285879} {:answer/id #uuid "dc679560-5667-5eba-bd15-c7313824d52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}-{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285880} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd78458-d203-54e5-940d-600f84a02ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffd78458-d203-54e5-940d-600f84a02ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285881} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de85bdb-bbc2-5658-8655-3bb0ab504047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa7d7027-df3b-5423-a3c5-4b5f8160bf07" :question/math-academy-id "q-170132" :question/problem "If $x=3{y}^{3}-4{y}^{5},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{3}-4{y}^{5}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5}) \\\\  & =9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc1cfa2-e77b-5df2-9230-d31b5ee7b961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285884} {:answer/id #uuid "e76968bb-2549-5bb7-b324-4acdd4794389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285885} {:answer/id #uuid "0b4a9813-c22d-5ac4-b345-e60feb489e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285886} {:answer/id #uuid "b82e4d60-7810-5484-ac36-49b2396d1af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285887} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc48167-c772-5b74-bc36-f32d5ea63466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddc48167-c772-5b74-bc36-f32d5ea63466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285888} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d438b7-e840-53c5-9b8a-f6d144a45862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbe5e0e9-59cc-550d-aeef-7d41dc23e22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-170140" :question/problem "If $x=y-2{y}^{3},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y-2{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =1-6{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1-6{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(1,-1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(1,-1)} & =\\frac{1}{1-6(-1)^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e99507-6c11-58bb-a6a9-aa455cb74c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{9}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285891} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c9b54d-4869-5374-9e3c-706e09913b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285892} {:answer/id #uuid "f209abb2-cb22-58c2-a498-92e507cfd39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{9}{2}x-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285893} {:answer/id #uuid "b4186441-3477-5355-b711-e2ab3e4ea40f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285894} {:answer/id #uuid "537727ee-4c0e-58f4-bd5e-382b7063d652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4186441-3477-5355-b711-e2ab3e4ea40f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285894} :answer-field/id #uuid "729cc38e-d4a8-5e5c-b785-16d5d6c7da25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d347d37d-5e79-5ebc-b87b-c0644c39f073" :question/math-academy-id "q-170190" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{y}^{3/2}}-4y \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-8{y}^{5/2}}{2{y}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-1,1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(1)\\sqrt{1}}{1+8(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{2}{9}(x-(-1)) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b74db806-be40-57af-a1b7-dc43cc750755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285898} {:answer/id #uuid "37be0d41-97a3-58d9-8233-f02797fba6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6x-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285899} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a557f9-6a8c-51f4-b4d1-4039834ac6f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285900} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f557ce-2eea-585f-80db-e54a1453d899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285901} {:answer/id #uuid "eee2b696-a3a6-59d4-8e91-da93d36cff2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f557ce-2eea-585f-80db-e54a1453d899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285901} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce113ae-7d3a-5121-b63f-cc4d2e99513e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d13262e-5677-5318-bc1a-cd98d393d979" :question/math-academy-id "q-170192" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2y)-2{y}^{-3}-0 \\\\  & =8y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8{y}^{4}-2}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)^{3}}{8(1)^{4}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{6}(x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134140fd-453d-5b29-9d53-1b1ecc5b01dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285905} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2dd8fb-895c-5f4e-94bd-f5b301271f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa2dd8fb-895c-5f4e-94bd-f5b301271f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ca3907-14b7-5e18-b658-b106098cb838" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4724076-8252-5361-8cdf-8e30f8695953" :question/math-academy-id "q-312549" :question/problem "Given that $x={y}^{2}-y,$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y) \\\\  & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2y-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bf8c22-1815-5984-b324-1e50de35ac88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285908} {:answer/id #uuid "518aa776-d87d-55cd-9744-3ff9f7678e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285909} {:answer/id #uuid "72e42b9d-701c-582e-aa32-29f816a3acef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285910} {:answer/id #uuid "f466adf4-43d5-56da-851f-a6e555037c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285911} {:answer/id #uuid "5265d538-86fb-56ae-8787-e354dec8b44d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "518aa776-d87d-55cd-9744-3ff9f7678e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285909} :answer-field/id #uuid "8285d5cd-97f2-5399-9f53-6c79532be8d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e944b722-89ed-5df5-8b31-cb3570eaaf1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32595" :question/problem "If $x=2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,9).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{-1/2}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2y\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{2y+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,9),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,9)} & =\\frac{2(9)\\sqrt{9}}{2(9)+3}=\\frac{18}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83cf3c48-4a08-5d76-9001-a12ff3eaf5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{x}{12} + \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117283} {:answer/id #uuid "ce685e16-28b1-5118-9b64-c6699b556246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 9x + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117284} {:answer/id #uuid "01357c03-93f7-5b00-9d6a-5b828298ccec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 12x - 27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117285} {:answer/id #uuid "04592928-f664-5e57-8649-5e015bfeeb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{x}{12} + \\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117286} {:answer/id #uuid "37f17073-53d1-533d-bc17-5d1086fb8ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{x}{12} + \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83cf3c48-4a08-5d76-9001-a12ff3eaf5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{x}{12} + \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117283} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e52567-654e-5366-a5d2-1c4d22b83b96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7ef2446-7ddb-53cb-83cf-b4fed6b4ea6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32596" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(9,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(3)^{2}-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{12}(x-9) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac{3}{4}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97afe22c-eb37-526a-94ff-17a86549f9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{4 + 4y^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117319} {:answer/id #uuid "bafdb32a-b4b0-564d-aa87-cc03a816e378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{1 + y^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117320} {:answer/id #uuid "fba014c2-926d-55fd-8f38-8d8294200fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4 + 4y^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117321} {:answer/id #uuid "00b0652b-e85a-56b4-9a59-954daa911f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{4 + 4y^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117322} {:answer/id #uuid "239ef000-5fbf-5756-99e7-0c934d95c643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3}}{1 + x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97afe22c-eb37-526a-94ff-17a86549f9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{4 + 4y^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117319} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a169c0b-f193-553b-9380-f8725bb03128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd82fd71-e11f-52b4-879b-d6f659d732bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-32705" :question/problem "If $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{-3}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c37f9256-da8a-5ba7-bd60-ed511c831190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+10y^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c37f9256-da8a-5ba7-bd60-ed511c831190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+10y^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285915} :answer-field/id #uuid "97d53035-97e0-582c-afb0-253e72579b34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05897e0d-06be-55d9-88a0-39032be05a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341608" :question/problem "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a567409-0509-531d-9d9e-e5a94596563b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a567409-0509-531d-9d9e-e5a94596563b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285918} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c11e239-c3af-5db3-a5b7-e9d39cb32a4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ddc71d8-aab5-5e88-9690-82c0e13ce162" :question/math-academy-id "q-341636" :question/problem "If $x=2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(20,2).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(3{y}^{2})+2y \\\\  & =6{y}^{2}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6{y}^{2}+2y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(20,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)} & =\\frac{1}{6({2}^{2})+2(2)}=\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2f80c6c-fdf9-588b-b84f-6a0f3d1a089a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f80c6c-fdf9-588b-b84f-6a0f3d1a089a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285921} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd43bec-34df-53b7-b316-a53d2403a1e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aada2aac-9808-566e-a932-6ee841bb6da4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341757" :question/problem "If $x=-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(-14,1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2y\\cdot {y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12(-\\frac{1}{2}){y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6{y}^{-3/2}-3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{y\\sqrt{y}}-3\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3{y}^{2}}{y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{y\\sqrt{y}}{6-3{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(-14,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{1}}{6-3(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90531a37-fc9e-5c9f-a16f-88465b373949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90531a37-fc9e-5c9f-a16f-88465b373949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285924} :answer-field/id #uuid "610faf0f-7729-5522-893e-0781abd865f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45e88e0a-eda2-5d07-9063-d301368f5fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-342049" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=2y-\\frac{6}{y},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-\\frac{6}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-6{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2(1)-6(-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+6{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}+6}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}+6}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2(3)^{2}+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x-\\frac{3}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e0f1a8c-0ef0-52c7-a098-fafd807d4a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285927} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e842ac-da9d-5a2e-b35d-3aa409a4b095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285928} {:answer/id #uuid "e8033fcd-d134-5dad-b539-cb7edfc6631a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285929} {:answer/id #uuid "f072ca5f-9a97-5334-affe-ea5072b01c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285930} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6dad1d-e156-5684-b74e-101cfc0b0d5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e0f1a8c-0ef0-52c7-a098-fafd807d4a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285927} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4ee07f-34bd-5d6c-a0e6-0da499fa1149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4928953b-0350-5f60-9789-334738000d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-51336" :question/problem "If $x=\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{-1}+8{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-{y}^{-2})+8\\cdot (-2{y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{-2}-16{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2y-16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y+16}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2y+16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,2)} & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{2(2)+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
